WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:12.200 --> 00:00:16.200
The upcoming Game of Thrones prequel series,
House of the Dragon, is based on the George

00:00:16.200 --> 00:00:21.650
RR Martin's Targaryen history book Fire &amp; Blood.
House of the Dragon is a Game of Thrones prequel

00:00:21.650 --> 00:00:25.900
show that is confirmed by HBO’s president
to air in 2022.

00:00:25.900 --> 00:00:31.320
Miguel Sapochnik and Ryan Condal will serve
as showrunners and executive producers. George

00:00:31.320 --> 00:00:33.960
R. R. Martin will also serve as executive
producer.

00:00:33.960 --> 00:00:40.480
It is based on George RR Martin’s book Fire
And Blood volume 1 and on Martin’s yet unfinished

00:00:40.480 --> 00:00:44.030
Fire And Blood volume 2 book.
“Fire &amp; Blood begins their tale with the

00:00:44.030 --> 00:00:48.900
legendary Aegon the Conqueror, creator of
the Iron Throne, and goes on to recount the

00:00:48.900 --> 00:00:53.650
generations of Targaryens who fought to hold
that iconic seat, all the way up to the civil

00:00:53.650 --> 00:00:58.530
war that nearly tore their dynasty apart.”
In other words it covers events from Aegon's

00:00:58.530 --> 00:01:02.920
Conquest to the Dance of the Dragons.
Thats Fire And Blood volume 1.

00:01:02.920 --> 00:01:08.250
The yet unreleased Fire And Vlood volume 2
will continue from where part 1 ended, with

00:01:08.250 --> 00:01:13.850
Rhaenyra Targaryen's son Aegon lll's reign
and will cover Blackyre rebellions, war with

00:01:13.850 --> 00:01:19.469
Dorne and go all the way to the Mad King and
Robert's Rebellion that ended Targaryen dynasty.

00:01:19.469 --> 00:01:23.710
But back to Aegon's Conquest.
King Torrhen Stark, also known as the King

00:01:23.710 --> 00:01:29.909
Who Knelt, was a head of House Stark who reigned
as King in the North when Aegon I Targaryen

00:01:29.909 --> 00:01:34.109
invaded Westeros with his dragons and started
the War of Conquest.

00:01:34.109 --> 00:01:39.959
Unlike every other king in Westeros, the King
in the North refused to fight Aegon but instead

00:01:39.959 --> 00:01:44.149
knelt before him, prioritizing his people
over his ego.

00:01:44.149 --> 00:01:48.459
He was the last King in the North until the
secession of the North and the Riverlands

00:01:48.459 --> 00:01:52.549
in the War of the Five Kings and the coronation
of Robb Stark.

00:01:52.549 --> 00:01:57.599
House Stark ruled as Kings in the North stretching
back into the mists of time, before written

00:01:57.599 --> 00:02:03.390
history began six thousand years ago, when
the Andals invaded all of southern Westeros.

00:02:03.390 --> 00:02:09.399
When the Andals arrived, the Stark Kings in
the North were already ruling at Winterfell.

00:02:09.399 --> 00:02:14.410
According to legend, the first King in the
North was Brandon Stark, better known as Bran

00:02:14.410 --> 00:02:20.180
the Builder, who lived eight thousand years
ago. According to legends, he led the forces

00:02:20.180 --> 00:02:25.349
of the North in the War for the Dawn against
the White Walkers and built the Wall to guard

00:02:25.349 --> 00:02:30.720
against their return, and also began construction
of Winterfell. The Kings in the North were

00:02:30.720 --> 00:02:35.390
successfully able to fend off the Andals from
invading, holding the line of the Neck at

00:02:35.390 --> 00:02:40.769
the choke point of Moat Cailin. As a result,
the North remained the only independent kingdom

00:02:40.769 --> 00:02:45.769
of the First Men. The North would be an independent
kingom until Aegon the Conqueror comes with

00:02:45.769 --> 00:02:50.540
his sisters and their dragons, and the unfortunate
Stark King who would rule the North at this

00:02:50.540 --> 00:02:56.150
time happened to be Torrhen Stark. Let's tell
the tale of the King Who Kneeled.

00:02:56.150 --> 00:03:00.760
After the riverlands and Storm's End had fallen
under the control of Aegon the Conqueror,

00:03:00.760 --> 00:03:06.650
Torrhen Stark called his banners. He was aware
that, due to the vast distance of the North,

00:03:06.650 --> 00:03:11.301
it would take a long time to assemble his
army. After the Field of Fire, which was the

00:03:11.301 --> 00:03:16.260
pivotal battle that decided the result of
the War of Conquest in which Kings Mern Gardener

00:03:16.260 --> 00:03:21.159
of the Reach and Loren Lannister of the Rock
faced the invading Aegon the Conqueror on

00:03:21.159 --> 00:03:25.960
the open field. The two kings combined the
armies of both the richest Kingdom and the

00:03:25.960 --> 00:03:33.400
most populous Kingdom, terming it the "Iron
Fist". Their total force numbered 60,000 men.

00:03:33.400 --> 00:03:38.470
In contrast, Aegon's army was outnumbered
by five to one. The battle was fought on a

00:03:38.470 --> 00:03:43.670
wide field in the Reach. However, Aegon the
Conqueror unleashed his three dragons against

00:03:43.670 --> 00:03:50.549
the enemy army. Four thousand men burned alive
that day, including King Mern himself. King

00:03:50.549 --> 00:03:56.239
Loren, instead, bent the knee to the Targaryen
warlord. He was thus appointed Lord Paramount

00:03:56.239 --> 00:04:01.270
of the Westerlands and Warden of the West.
With the death of King Mern, House Gardener,

00:04:01.270 --> 00:04:06.450
which had ruled the Reach since the time of
the First Men, became extinct. House Tyrell,

00:04:06.450 --> 00:04:12.480
the hereditary stewards of the Gardeners,
then surrendered Highgarden to Aegon. In return,

00:04:12.480 --> 00:04:17.049
Aegon raised Harlen Tyrell, the head of the
family, to Lord Paramount of the Reach and

00:04:17.049 --> 00:04:22.750
Warden of the South. While at Highgarden,
Aegon I learned that Torrhen had crossed the

00:04:22.750 --> 00:04:28.720
Neck and entered the riverlands, leading an
army of thirty thousand men. Torrhen amassed

00:04:28.720 --> 00:04:35.280
his army and marched to meet the Targaryen
warlord. Aegon I abandoned his plans to march

00:04:35.280 --> 00:04:40.690
south, and at once started his way north,
racing ahead of his army on Balerion. Both

00:04:40.690 --> 00:04:45.670
Rhaenys and Visenya Targaryen, as well as
all the lords who had bent the knee to Aegon

00:04:45.670 --> 00:04:50.970
after Harrenhal and the Field of Fire, were
sent word of this movement. So when Torrhen

00:04:50.970 --> 00:04:56.190
reached the banks of the Trident, he found
a host of forty-five thousand men and three

00:04:56.190 --> 00:05:02.420
dragons waiting for him. After seeing Aegon's
dragons and his massive host, Torrhen realized

00:05:02.420 --> 00:05:08.940
the war was already lost. Even without dragons,
Torrhen Stark and his northerners were outnumbered,

00:05:08.940 --> 00:05:13.730
but there was no doubt he would give a good
fight against those odds but when he saw three

00:05:13.730 --> 00:05:18.700
dragons of Aegon the Conqueror, he spent the
entire night with his generals thinking of

00:05:18.700 --> 00:05:23.390
what his next and perhaps his final move as
the King in the North should be. Torrhen's

00:05:23.390 --> 00:05:28.420
scouts had reported seeing the ruins of Harrenhal,
and Torrhen had heard accounts of the Field

00:05:28.420 --> 00:05:33.920
of Fire as well. Some of his lords urged him
to attack, but he realized that a similar

00:05:33.920 --> 00:05:39.700
fate would await him, if he tried to force
a crossing. Others of his lords urged the

00:05:39.700 --> 00:05:45.850
King of the North to fall back to Moat Cailin,
to make his stand there. Torrhen's bastard

00:05:45.850 --> 00:05:51.020
half-brother, Brandon Snow, offered to cross
the Trident at dark, to kill the dragons.

00:05:51.020 --> 00:05:56.380
At the end, Torrhen did send his half-brother
Brandon Snow to Aegon's camp, but not to kill

00:05:56.380 --> 00:06:01.660
Aegon's dragons, but to treat with Aegon.
The whole night, messages went back and forth,

00:06:01.660 --> 00:06:05.660
and the next morning, Torrhen crossed the
Trident, where he kneeled and laid his crown

00:06:05.660 --> 00:06:11.301
at the feet of Aegon I Targaryen, and swore
fealty. In exchange for his life, and the

00:06:11.301 --> 00:06:16.810
lives of the Northmen, Torrhen Stark swore
fealty to House Targaryen. Instead of fighting,

00:06:16.810 --> 00:06:20.150
he chose to bend the knee and surrendered
his crown.

00:06:20.150 --> 00:06:24.500
In return for Torrhen's submission, Aegon
allowed House Stark to continue ruling the

00:06:24.500 --> 00:06:29.470
North as they had for thousands of years,
but as vassals of the Iron Throne. They held

00:06:29.470 --> 00:06:34.160
the titles of Lord Paramount of the North,
Lord of Winterfell, and Warden of the North.

00:06:34.160 --> 00:06:39.660
The Starks thus retained their ancient positions
and traditions. Ever since, Torrhen is known

00:06:39.660 --> 00:06:45.200
as the King Who Kneeled. It's unknown what
Aegon did with Torrhen's crown. The Inn of

00:06:45.200 --> 00:06:49.430
the Kneeling Man later arose where Torrhen
had bent the knee.

00:06:49.430 --> 00:06:54.140
After Torrhen's surrender, the Company of
the Rose, a sellsword company, was formed

00:06:54.140 --> 00:06:58.930
by men and (according to some accounts) women
from the North who refused to bend the knee

00:06:58.930 --> 00:07:05.460
to Aegon I Targaryen. These men and women
willingly chose exile across the Narrow Sea.

00:07:05.460 --> 00:07:10.400
Torrhen's sons did not agree with the Targaryen
rule. Some of them spoke of rebelling, and

00:07:10.400 --> 00:07:16.390
raising the Stark banner. Whether Torrhen
gave his consent or not is unknown. No rebellions

00:07:16.390 --> 00:07:21.551
by House Stark are known thus far. Lord Torrhen's
daughter was married to Ronnel Arryn, Lord

00:07:21.551 --> 00:07:27.300
of the Eyrie. This marriage had been arranged
by Queen Rhaenys Targaryen as an attempt to

00:07:27.300 --> 00:07:32.210
knit the new realm together. There are letters
at the Citadel which suggest that Lord Stark

00:07:32.210 --> 00:07:37.400
only agreed to this match after much protest,
and that his sons had refused to attend the

00:07:37.400 --> 00:07:42.440
wedding. Lord Ronnel would be killed early
in the reign of King Aenys I Targaryen by

00:07:42.440 --> 00:07:47.130
his own brother, Jonos. It’s unknown whether
Torrhen's daughter was still alive at this

00:07:47.130 --> 00:07:51.930
point. Torrhen was entombed in the crypts
of Winterfell after his death.

00:07:51.930 --> 00:07:56.550
Three centuries later, Torrhen's descendant,
Ned Stark was amongst the rebel lords against

00:07:56.550 --> 00:08:01.820
Aegon the Conqueror's descendant Aerys the
Mad King during Robert's Rebellion, in which

00:08:01.820 --> 00:08:08.060
the Targaryen dynasty was deposed and Robert
crowned as the new king. Although some Northerners

00:08:08.060 --> 00:08:13.430
sneer at Torrhen as "the king who knelt",
his descendants, the Starks, argue that Torrhen

00:08:13.430 --> 00:08:18.540
"saved thousands of lives that day" and that
his critics forget that they are alive today

00:08:18.540 --> 00:08:23.000
because of him. King Torrhen is mentioned
a few times in Game of Thrones for kneeling

00:08:23.000 --> 00:08:28.870
down to Aegon and his dragons. The most significant
mention of the King Who Knelt was in season

00:08:28.870 --> 00:08:33.159
7. When Jon Snow appears before Daenerys Targaryen
on Dragonstone,

00:08:33.159 --> 00:08:37.710
the latter scoffs when Ser Davos Seaworth
presents Jon as the King in the North and

00:08:37.710 --> 00:08:42.300
declares that the last person who held that
title was Torrhen Stark, who bent the knee

00:08:42.300 --> 00:08:47.790
to her ancestor, Aegon the Conqueror, using
Torrhen's declaration of loyalty in perpetuity

00:08:47.790 --> 00:08:53.580
to try and persuade Jon into confirming the
North's fealty to House Targaryen and abandoning

00:08:53.580 --> 00:08:59.220
the King in the North title. King in the North
(feminine equivalent being Queen in the North)

00:08:59.220 --> 00:09:04.560
is the title given to the ruler of the North
during its time as an independent kingdom,

00:09:04.560 --> 00:09:09.450
before and after the coming of the Targaryens.
A title also used for the rulers of the North

00:09:09.450 --> 00:09:14.750
was the "Kings of Winter". During the opening
stages of the War of the Five Kings, Lord

00:09:14.750 --> 00:09:19.880
Robb Stark was proclaimed as the new King
in the North by his bannermen, the first in

00:09:19.880 --> 00:09:25.150
300 years after Torrhen Stark. The "Kingdom
of the North" came to a temporary end after

00:09:25.150 --> 00:09:30.750
the Red Wedding when Roose Bolton, who conspired
with House Frey and House Lannister, initiated

00:09:30.750 --> 00:09:35.890
a massacre of the northern army and personally
stabbed Robb Stark through the heart. However,

00:09:35.890 --> 00:09:41.520
the "Kingdom of the North" was reestablished
after a short few years under the Bolton rule,

00:09:41.520 --> 00:09:47.010
when the Starks led by Jon Snow and Sansa
Stark later gathered an army of Northern houses

00:09:47.010 --> 00:09:51.500
still loyal to House Stark, the Free Folk,
and the Knights of the Vale and retook Winterfell

00:09:51.500 --> 00:09:56.360
from the Boltons. With the Boltons defeated,
Jon Snow was proclaimed the new King in the

00:09:56.360 --> 00:10:01.110
North, reasserting the North's independence
from the Iron Throne. The "Kingdom of the

00:10:01.110 --> 00:10:06.250
North" came to a temporary end once again
when Jon bent the knee to Queen Daenerys Targaryen

00:10:06.250 --> 00:10:11.960
in order to gain her full support in the Great
War. Like Torrhen Stark, Jon Snow bent the

00:10:11.960 --> 00:10:18.380
knee to save his people. After the death of
Daenerys Targaryen, Sansa Stark declared independence

00:10:18.380 --> 00:10:22.690
from the Iron Throne and herself the Queen
in the North and thus the "Kingdom in the

00:10:22.690 --> 00:10:28.860
North" was reestablished once again. Her brother
Bran Stark became the ruler of the Six Kingdoms.

00:10:28.860 --> 00:10:35.000
300 years after Torrhen Stark knelt to Aegon
Targaryen, now Aegon's descendant Jon Snow

00:10:35.000 --> 00:10:40.830
who's real name is Aegon kneeled down to Torrhen's
descendant Bran. All of this is part of the

00:10:40.830 --> 00:10:45.460
Targaryen history and the upcoming Game of
Thrones prequel, House of the Dragon is based

00:10:45.460 --> 00:10:49.120
on the Targaryen history.
We are bound for an epic journey starting

00:10:49.120 --> 00:10:54.440
in 2022 which is when the first episode of
the Game of Thrones prequel airs. Thank you

00:10:54.440 --> 00:10:56.650
so much for watching, hope you enjoyed this
video and if you did make sure to give it

00:10:56.650 --> 00:10:58.820
a big thumbs up and I hope to see you in the
next one, peace!

